  data:  # a7c6
    kind: work_item  # a7c6
    title: "The State A/B/C classification that justifies the pass-silence axis exists only in prose; its one branching consumer re-derives it as '!= no_candidate_files', which will misclassify the next value added"  # a7c6
    status: todo_hard  # a7c6
    priority: 3  # a7c6
    parent:  # a7c6
    tags:  # a7c6
    - analysis_quality  # a7c6
    - disclosure  # a7c6
    isbefore: []  # a7c6
    duplicate_of: []  # a7c6
    not_duplicate_of: []  # a7c6
    pr_ref:  # a7c6
    description: "Found by the 2026-09-17 fundamental concept audit of the pass-silence host\nboundary (Test 4, mechanism vs category). Write-up:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-pass-silence-host-boundary_09172026.md\n\nTHE GAP. pass_silence.py opens by declaring the entire reason the axis exists:\n\n    A  ran, and there was genuinely nothing to find   (correct, uninteresting)\n    B  ran, and could not find what was there         (a recall defect)\n    C  did not really run -- a prerequisite was absent (an ordering defect)\n\nTHAT CLASSIFICATION EXISTS ONLY IN PROSE COMMENTS. Grepped the whole tree: the\nstrings \"State A/B/C\" appear in pass_silence.py docstrings and one comment in\nlinkers/registry.py, and nowhere as data. No value->state mapping is exported.\nSILENCE_REASONS is a flat frozenset of 8 strings.\n\nSo a consumer cannot ask the only question that matters operationally -- \"would\ninstalling something, or reordering something, change this?\" -- without\nhardcoding a set.\n\nAND ONE CONSUMER ALREADY DOES, at n=1. prerequisite_absent_clauses:\n\n    if any(skip_reason_codes[literal] != NO_CANDIDATE_FILES for literal in clause)\n\nThat is \"is this a toolchain reason\" re-derived as \"is it not the one file\nreason\". It is correct today because the skip host only ever carries\n{no_candidate_files, dependency_unavailable, backend_disabled, pass_crashed,\nunreported}. It silently classifies ANY NEW VALUE as a toolchain reason. The\nvocabulary has grown 6 -> 7 (ADR-0054) -> 8 (ADR-0056) in two months, so \"a\nninth value\" is not hypothetical.\n\nThis is the playbook's \"hardcoded set enumerating variants\" anti-pattern,\ncaught while it is still one line long.\n\nPROPOSED SHAPE: export the state alongside the value (a frozen-dataclass spec\nlist like edge_types.py, per the axis-declaration template's \"consumer pattern\"\nartifact), and replace the proxy with a call against it. The registry module\nalready exists; it just holds a bare frozenset.\n\n=== TWO LATENT TRAPS ON THE SAME FUNCTION, recorded so they are not rediscovered ===\n\n(1) \"\" HAS NO DECLARED MEANING ON THE SKIP HOST. On AnalysisRun, \"\" is\nemphatically NOT APPLICABLE, and pass_silence.py argues at length that\ncollapsing it with `unreported` (CANNOT DETERMINE) would repeat a defect the\nproject has already paid for. On the skip host, two consumers of the same field\ndisagree about absence:\n\n    pass_silence.summarize_skip_reasons   missing code -> UNREPORTED\n    linkers/registry.py:916               missing code -> \"\"\n\nNo observable wrong answer today: both fall on the same side of the\n!= NO_CANDIDATE_FILES partition, and all four producer sites write a code, so\n\"\" is presently unreachable in production. RE-OPEN TRIGGER: the moment any\nproducer writes a skipped_passes entry without a skip_reason_code, or a fifth\nproducer site is added.\n\n(2) THE DOCUMENTED BLIND SPOT IS UNDERSTATED. prerequisite_absent_clauses's\ndocstring says only linkers are unobservable (\"Only ANALYZER passes are\nenumerated in limits.skipped_passes\"), and its Args section says \"A pass absent\nfrom this mapping ran.\" Both are false for the 26 out-of-taxonomy analyzers that\nland in analysis_runs with zero files (see the sibling spec row) -- apex, twig,\nmake, manifest_targets and 22 others are declared prerequisites that can never\nbe observed missing.\n\nBENIGN TODAY, and I traced both branches rather than assuming: a clause needs\nEVERY literal present in the map to qualify, so an out-of-taxonomy literal with\nzero files simply fails the `all(...)` guard and no stamp is due -- which is the\nsame outcome the in-taxonomy path reaches by contributing a file reason. NOT\nproven exhaustively: I checked the zero-file case, not that no clause shape can\ndiverge."  # a7c6
    fields: {}  # a7c6
- op: discuss  # fc9a
