  nonce: fc9a  # fc9a
  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 9245df71d6 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures, scratchpad stale1025b/repro_<ID>/). CURRENT, refs drifted, premise STRONGER. Probe: still 8 values, no value->state export; prerequisite_absent_clauses' proxy (pass_silence.py:709-711, parameter now silence_reasons) maps every value except no_candidate_files to State C, including no_candidate_construct (State A) and any new string. ADDITIONS: (a) ROUTINE_SILENCE_REASONS (WI-vadom, pass_silence.py:208) is a SECOND hand-written partition of the same vocabulary and disagrees with the proxy on backend_disabled (routine there, toolchain in the proxy) -- two consumers now, not one. (b) Live: with tree-sitter-language-pack absent, a python-only repo reports dependency_unavailable for 29 out-of-taxonomy passes with zero files -- State A by the module's own definitions -- so the state depends on value AND file presence; the exported mapping must take both. (c) WI-nijil (crashed linkers invisible to dependents) fixes the same docstring (:683-690, :696-697) from the linker side, and its fix feeds linker records into the map this proxy reads: this item is now ordered before WI-nijil. Trap (1)'s trigger has not fired (all 4 skip producers write a code: all_analyzers.py:232/245/368, limits.py:160); '' default now linkers/registry.py:1011. Trap (2) is live: apex/twig/manifest_targets/play-routes/yaml_ansible are depends_on literals hosted in analysis_runs. P3 kept."  # fc9a
